# Copy to .env for local development.
#
# Absolute base URL of the API, including the /api prefix. Setting this makes
# the browser call the backend directly, which is cross-origin — the app's own
# origin must therefore be listed in the backend's CLIENT_ORIGIN.
#
# Leave it unset to call the app's own origin instead (`/api`). In `vite dev`
# and `vite preview` that is proxied to the target in vite.config.ts; in
# production it assumes a reverse proxy serves the API from the same origin.
#
# Vite inlines this at build time, so a production build needs it set at build
# time, not at runtime.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4100/api
